<file path="docs/man/doit.1">
.TH DOIT 1 "September 2026" "DoIT" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
doit \- A sleek CLI task manager tool built with Go and WASM SQLite3
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B doit
.IR command " [" options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B doit
is a command-line todo/task manager that stores its data in a local SQLite
database (see
.B init
and
.B DBPATH
below). Tasks live in one of four logical lists:
.IR todos ,
.IR completed ,
.IR trash ,
and
.IR ignored .
.SH INITIALIZATION
Before using
.B doit
in a directory tree, you must initialize a repository:
.PP
.B doit init
.PP
This creates a
.B .doit/
directory containing the SQLite database
.B doit.db
in the current working directory. Every later
.B doit
command looks for
.B .doit/
by starting from the current directory and walking upward, so commands will
only work when run inside (or below) an initialized project.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR init
Create a new
.B .doit
repository in the current directory.
.TP
.BR add " | " a " " \fItask\fP
Add a new todo. Exactly one task argument is accepted.
.TP
.BR list " | " ls
List all active todos. Tasks are numbered starting from index 0; these
indices (not database row ids) are the ids used by other commands.
.TP
.BR done " | " d " " \fIid\fP
Mark the todo at list index
.I id
as done, moving it to the
.IR completed
list.
.TP
.BR remove " | " rm " " \fIid\fP
Prompt for confirmation, then move the todo at list index
.I id
to the
.IR trash
list.
.TP
.BR completed " | " c " " \fIsubcommand\fP
Operate on the completed list. Subcommands:
.RS
.TP
.BR list " | " ls
List completed tasks.
.TP
.BR remove " | " rm " " \fIid\fP
Permanently delete the task at index
.I id
from the completed list (cannot be recovered).
.TP
.BR nuke " | " n
Prompt for confirmation, then permanently clear all completed tasks.
.RE
.TP
.BR trash " | " t " " \fIsubcommand\fP
Operate on the trash list. Subcommands:
.RS
.TP
.BR list " | " ls
List tasks in trash.
.TP
.BR remove " | " rm " " \fIid\fP
Permanently delete the task at index
.I id
from the trash (cannot be recovered).
.TP
.BR nuke " | " n
Prompt for confirmation, then permanently clear the entire trash.
.RE
.TP
.BR ignored " | " i " " \fIsubcommand\fP
Operate on the ignored list. Subcommands:
.RS
.TP
.BR list " | " ls
List ignored tasks.
.TP
.BR remove " | " rm " " \fIid\fP
Permanently delete the task at index
.I id
from the ignored list (cannot be recovered).
.TP
.BR nuke " | " n
Prompt for confirmation, then permanently clear all ignored tasks.
.RE
.TP
.BR move " | " mv " " \fI<t|c|i>\fP " " \fIid\fP " [" \fI<t|c|i>\fP "]"
Move a task between the trash, completed, and ignored lists. The first
source argument
.I <t|c|i>
selects the source list (one of
.IR trash ,
.IR completed ,
.IR ignored
or their single-letter aliases), and
.I id
is the 0-based index within that list. With no target argument, the task is
moved back to
.IR todos .
With an explicit target
.I <t|c|i>
it is moved to that list instead.
.SH DBPATH
By default
.B doit
writes its database to
.B .doit/doit.db
relative to the directory where
.B doit init
was run. The connection is opened with WAL journal mode and foreign keys
enabled.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS
doit init
doit add "buy milk"
doit list
doit d 0            # mark the first listed todo done
doit c list         # show completed tasks
doit t list         # show trashed tasks
doit mv t 0 c       # move the first trashed task to completed
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .doit/doit.db
The SQLite database created by
.BR "doit init" .
.SH BUGS
Multi-session support is not yet fully active; the runtime session is hardcoded to
.IR todo .
.SH AUTHOR
Adarasha Gaihre (aakku) <aakku@adarashagaihre.com.np>
.SH HOME
Website: https://adarashagaihre.com.np
.br
Source: https://github.com/aakku106/DoIT
.SH COPYRIGHT
Copyright (C) 2026 Adarasha Gaihre (aakku).
.PP
This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it
under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the Free
Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or (at your option)
any later version.
</file>

<file path="docs/prompt.md">
# DoIT — Project Brief (for AI)

Go CLI todo app. SQLite via `ncruces/go-sqlite3` (WASM). Typed query layer generated by `sqlc`.

## Stack
- Go 1.25+, SQLite (WAL), `sqlc` codegen.
- Entrypoint: `cmd/todo/main.go`. Handlers: `internal/cli/commands.go`. Store: `internal/store/` (generated). DB: `internal/db/sqlite.go`.

## Data
Four tables — `todos`, `completed`, `trash`, `ignored`. Each: `id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY`, `session TEXT` (hardcoded `"todo"`), `title TEXT`, timestamp columns. Schema truth: `sql/schema.sql` (embedded via `//go:embed`). Queries truth: `sql/queries.sql`. Migrations dir is stale — do not use.

## Key rules (agents must know)
1. **CLI IDs are display indices** (0-based, per `ls` output), NEVER DB row ids. Handlers map them through `ListTodoIDs`/`ListCompletedIDs`/`ListTrashIDs`/`ListIgnoredIDs`.
2. **Never hand-edit `internal/store/`** — generated. Edit `sql/*.sql` then `sqlc generate`.
3. **DB discovery walks upward** from cwd looking for `.doit/`. Must run `doit init` first; database is `.doit/doit.db`.
4. Session is **hardcoded** `"todo"` everywhere; multi-session stubbed via `sessionCall(args)` (empty).

## Commands
- `init` — create `.doit/` + DB.
- `add|a <task>` (`add` requires exactly one arg).
- `list|ls`, `done|d <id>`, `remove|rm <id>`.
- `completed|c [list|remove|nuke]`, `trash|t [...]`, `ignored|i [...]`.
- `move|mv <t|c|i> <id> <t|c|i>` — move between trash/completed/ignored.
- Anything else → `sessionCall` placeholder.

## Build / Run
```bash
go build -o doit ./cmd/todo
go run ./cmd/todo add "task"
./dev-build.sh   # dev build to ~/go/bin/xdoit
```

## Release / CI
- `.github/workflows/release.yml` + `.goreleaser.yaml`: cross-compiles `doit` for Linux/macOS/Windows on amd64/arm64; on **`v*` tag pushes** builds, attaches archives to GitHub release, and publishes a Homebrew formula to `aakku106/homebrew-tap` (binary + manpage). Needs `GITHUB_TOKEN` + `HOMEBREW_TAP_TOKEN` secrets.
- Manpage: `docs/man/doit.1`.
- README: `README.md` (root).

## State
- `internal/todo/service.go`: unused stub.
- `temp/`: sandbox, not part of app.
- No tests, no linter.
- `db.NewSQLite` has leftover debug print/log noise in `findDoitDir`.
- License: GPLv3 — keep header on all source files.
</file>

